WEBVTT

00:32.908 --> 00:33.909
Impossible...

00:35.827 --> 00:37.704
There's no way this is possible.

00:38.163 --> 00:41.875
No one can possibly get stronger from
a thing as vague as liking something.

00:42.417 --> 00:43.335
I...

00:43.669 --> 00:45.295
love Shizuka!

00:46.088 --> 00:47.797
She might be hasty, reckless,

00:47.798 --> 00:49.174
and a bit meek...

00:49.383 --> 00:50.801
But she's kinder
than anyone else.

00:51.426 --> 00:54.930
And on top of that, when things
get rough or don't go her way,

00:55.264 --> 00:57.015
she always stays
true to what she loves.

00:57.808 --> 01:01.520
Seeing her makes me
want to try harder myself too!

01:02.187 --> 01:05.691
A person's love can ignite
strength in those around them.

01:06.233 --> 01:09.027
You're trying to steal her love!

01:11.154 --> 01:14.616
That's the same
as stealing from me!

01:14.783 --> 01:16.618
Stop yapping!

01:22.833 --> 01:28.547
Compared to the pain of
losing the things you love...

01:29.089 --> 01:32.384
a punch like that is nothing!

01:40.851 --> 01:42.144
- Suzuri-san!
- You okay?!

01:45.022 --> 01:46.940
Don't worry, get back.

01:48.233 --> 01:49.443
What's goin' on?

01:49.860 --> 01:53.030
They didn't give a damn about
their teammates goin' down,

01:53.405 --> 01:55.032
but they care about him?

01:55.866 --> 01:57.409
Sheesh.

01:58.076 --> 02:00.996
You just keep yapping
on and on and on,

02:01.622 --> 02:05.209
but all you spout is...

02:05.751 --> 02:08.504
idealistic crap you
only find in video games.

02:21.141 --> 02:24.143
Unfulfilled

02:24.144 --> 02:26.979
Self-centered emotion

02:26.980 --> 02:29.565
Dodging away

02:29.566 --> 02:31.651
Bring it on, cutting
through the wind

02:31.652 --> 02:34.403
Nothing to lose

02:34.404 --> 02:37.114
Nothing to protect

02:37.115 --> 02:39.909
Howling voice someday

02:39.910 --> 02:41.786
Fly away into the blue sky

02:41.787 --> 02:43.746
Just tell me everything

02:43.747 --> 02:46.833
Searching for the answer

02:46.834 --> 02:49.001
Even if they call it reckless

02:49.002 --> 02:51.754
I don't care

02:51.755 --> 02:54.340
Now, open the door

02:54.341 --> 02:57.301
Desperate comeback,
desired future

02:57.302 --> 03:01.931
Reach out, pull it closer

03:01.932 --> 03:04.684
This is my revolution, just

03:04.685 --> 03:07.687
Keep moving forward

03:07.688 --> 03:12.233
Even fate, piece by piece

03:12.234 --> 03:13.484
Get out of the way

03:13.485 --> 03:14.777
I'm gonna do it, alright?

03:14.778 --> 03:16.028
No reason, no proof

03:16.029 --> 03:18.614
Anyone blocking my
way, no more chances

03:18.615 --> 03:20.908
Rise up as a hero who
doesn't even look like one

03:20.909 --> 03:21.701
Laugh it off

03:21.702 --> 03:23.620
Together, prove my story, yeah

03:24.162 --> 03:26.831
Strength to protect someone

03:26.832 --> 03:29.500
Carved into this heart

03:29.501 --> 03:32.128
Like walking a tightrope

03:32.129 --> 03:34.673
Climb to the top

03:43.056 --> 03:44.057
Thanks!

03:44.224 --> 03:47.185
When you split a cookie
between six people,

03:47.186 --> 03:49.103
I guess everyone
just gets a crumb.

03:49.104 --> 03:51.231
I hope we won't have
more people to share it with.

03:51.732 --> 03:53.442
It's fine if we do.

03:54.234 --> 03:55.860
It doesn't matter
how many we are,

03:55.861 --> 03:57.196
we'll just split it equally.

03:58.488 --> 04:01.617
The only proper meal we
got was from school lunches.

04:02.075 --> 04:04.995
I can't even remember the
last time I had a full stomach.

04:06.246 --> 04:08.373
All the kids here
are in the same boat.

04:09.208 --> 04:11.877
Leave us alone, and we'd end
up fighting over a single cookie.

04:12.586 --> 04:14.630
I couldn't stand that.

04:15.797 --> 04:17.006
If we're gonna be hungry,

04:17.007 --> 04:19.718
I'd rather we starve
together while smiling.

04:20.677 --> 04:22.054
Thanks to everyone here,

04:22.387 --> 04:24.014
I was never alone.

04:25.057 --> 04:27.392
Looking back, I
was pretty naive.

04:27.601 --> 04:29.061
I believed that
someday, somehow,

04:29.436 --> 04:32.856
my world would
become fun and bright,

04:33.148 --> 04:36.401
like the ones I saw
on game posters.

04:37.569 --> 04:40.614
But reality only got worse.

04:40.989 --> 04:43.367
More and more
people wanted a crumb,

04:43.825 --> 04:46.620
and each person's
share kept shrinking.

04:47.496 --> 04:49.748
And one day, I realized.

04:50.457 --> 04:53.752
Nobody in this town had
the leeway to save anyone.

04:54.419 --> 04:58.131
No matter how long I wait, the fun
and bright game world will never come.

04:58.549 --> 05:00.843
And no matter how much
we cry over our suffering,

05:01.009 --> 05:02.886
our stomachs will never be full.

05:03.512 --> 05:06.974
I had to change
this crappy reality.

05:07.558 --> 05:08.976
You wanna make a team?

05:09.226 --> 05:10.185
Yeah.

05:10.394 --> 05:11.978
If we don't do anything,

05:11.979 --> 05:13.980
we'll only die a
pointless, miserable death.

05:13.981 --> 05:15.773
That's easier said than done.

05:15.774 --> 05:18.485
What're we supposed
to do? We've got nothing.

05:18.735 --> 05:20.612
But we do have
something: numbers.

05:22.155 --> 05:23.991
We can sell that
and get jobs for it.

05:24.366 --> 05:27.870
Whatever the payment, we
split it equally among our team.

05:28.078 --> 05:29.663
That'll be our only rule.

05:29.997 --> 05:32.039
That way, even
if one of us falls,

05:32.040 --> 05:34.668
someone else will make up
for it, and everyone will benefit.

05:35.586 --> 05:38.130
We'll become one unit.

05:39.131 --> 05:40.424
Just believe in me.

05:41.425 --> 05:45.053
After that, we did anything we could
with our numbers as our selling point.

05:45.637 --> 05:47.763
Whenever teams got into fights,

05:47.764 --> 05:50.517
we'd go to both sides and
have them bid for our help.

05:51.059 --> 05:52.685
If a person needed to be found,

05:52.686 --> 05:54.897
we'd use our numbers to
check every possible spot.

05:55.314 --> 05:57.316
And before long,
we got more jobs,

05:57.649 --> 05:59.776
and stopped fighting
among ourselves.

06:00.319 --> 06:01.445
This is good.

06:01.737 --> 06:03.238
This is what I wanted.

06:03.822 --> 06:05.656
Everyone's had enough to eat,

06:05.657 --> 06:07.534
and everyone's getting along.

06:07.868 --> 06:08.869
All's good.

06:09.203 --> 06:10.370
This is all I ever wanted.

06:10.913 --> 06:13.248
I don't care if we have
to take from others.

06:13.874 --> 06:16.752
This is the only
path we can walk.

06:17.419 --> 06:22.257
Reality isn't like video games.
Magic or miracles don't exist here!

06:25.177 --> 06:28.388
You talk about
how painful loss is,

06:28.722 --> 06:31.225
but only folks who have
something to lose get to say that!

06:32.267 --> 06:34.895
Sadly, I've never had
anything to begin with.

06:35.729 --> 06:36.730
That's why...

06:36.897 --> 06:39.775
I bet you're jealous of Shizuka.

06:40.359 --> 06:44.279
No matter what you say...

06:44.571 --> 06:47.157
People who mock
what other people love

06:47.449 --> 06:49.910
are usually just
unhappy with themselves.

06:50.577 --> 06:53.372
it might as well be static!

07:04.424 --> 07:06.134
Static, huh?

07:06.635 --> 07:08.887
Then why do you
look like you're in pain?

07:10.973 --> 07:13.183
Looks like I was
wrong about you.

07:13.934 --> 07:16.144
You're shouldering
pain too, aren't you?

07:16.770 --> 07:20.023
I really want to
understand you now.

07:20.649 --> 07:22.901
Tell me more about yourself.

07:24.027 --> 07:26.572
DON'T SCREW WITH ME!

07:28.615 --> 07:31.243
I've never seen Suzuri-san
look so desperate!

07:31.493 --> 07:33.412
Th-The whole
atmosphere's changed...

07:36.081 --> 07:38.417
Fighting's a type of
communication, Sakura-kun.

07:38.834 --> 07:40.627
So even Tsubakino can do that.

07:49.636 --> 07:52.096
Whaddya mean I'm
shouldering pain too?!

07:52.097 --> 07:53.557
You don't know a thing about me!

07:53.765 --> 07:57.978
Those who have will never
understand those who haven't!

07:58.937 --> 08:01.064
"Never understand," you say?

08:01.565 --> 08:03.150
Of course, I can't!

08:04.484 --> 08:07.404
It's not like you
understand me either!

08:07.696 --> 08:10.199
Different backgrounds
mean different mindsets!

08:10.616 --> 08:14.286
No one can truly understand
what someone else is going through!

08:14.745 --> 08:17.372
But I do know
you've got it rough!

08:17.623 --> 08:21.710
It's got nothing to do with
birth, gender, or what we have!

08:22.169 --> 08:26.507
Hard times hit hardest for
the ones going through them.

08:27.090 --> 08:28.467
But even so,

08:28.800 --> 08:33.680
I won't let you trample and take
away another person's love or passion.

08:34.306 --> 08:36.683
So I'm taking you down.

08:45.859 --> 08:46.943
S-Suzuri-san—

08:46.944 --> 08:48.028
Stay away!

08:50.697 --> 08:51.907
I can't lose.

08:52.449 --> 08:54.826
If I do, we'll be back
to where we started.

08:55.452 --> 08:57.454
We've come so far.

08:57.829 --> 08:59.623
I can't let it go to waste.

09:10.050 --> 09:11.593
...wh...y...

09:13.470 --> 09:15.430
...m-move...

09:19.101 --> 09:20.102
I'm sorry.

09:23.939 --> 09:25.524
What...?

09:26.108 --> 09:31.530
I may be doing what I love
now, but it wasn't always like this.

09:32.406 --> 09:34.073
I was like you in the past.

09:34.074 --> 09:35.534
It was rough.

09:36.159 --> 09:39.037
But there were
people who helped me.

09:39.663 --> 09:42.916
The reason why I am who I
am today is thanks to them.

09:44.751 --> 09:46.127
So what?!

09:46.128 --> 09:48.172
Want me to congratulate
you or something?!

09:51.341 --> 09:56.597
I don't know the details of why
you don't have anything you like.

09:57.389 --> 10:03.687
But I can see you're hurting,
just like I was back then.

10:04.396 --> 10:07.816
That's why I want to help you.

10:08.859 --> 10:11.987
Tell me what I can do
for you. It can be anything.

10:16.658 --> 10:18.076
Tsubaki-chan...

10:18.368 --> 10:20.871
Sheesh, that's
just like Tsubaki.

10:22.497 --> 10:23.415
What are you...

10:23.540 --> 10:25.708
The fact that you're in
pain for having nothing,

10:25.709 --> 10:27.878
means you want to
have something, right?

10:28.462 --> 10:31.381
There has to be something
you like or want to do.

10:31.924 --> 10:34.218
If it's within my
power, I'll do it.

10:34.760 --> 10:37.262
Let's do what you
want to do, together!

10:40.891 --> 10:42.434
How many times
do I have to tell you?

10:42.684 --> 10:44.603
Everything you say is
just idealistic bullshit.

10:45.062 --> 10:47.523
If you save me, then
what? What about them?

10:48.023 --> 10:51.234
There isn't a proper job
out there for folks like us!

10:51.235 --> 10:53.319
How are we supposed
to chase our dreams

10:53.320 --> 10:55.864
when we're too busy worrying
when our next meal's coming?!

10:59.368 --> 11:00.619
That reminds me,

11:00.953 --> 11:05.207
I think the manager was
looking for some extra hands.

11:08.669 --> 11:12.463
The ramen shop's
short on staff too.

11:12.464 --> 11:17.051
There's a store opening on 2nd Street,
but they don't have enough people yet.

11:17.052 --> 11:20.430
I've heard people saying
they've wanted to expand too.

11:20.931 --> 11:22.139
Wh-Why?

11:22.140 --> 11:23.684
Don't get us wrong.

11:24.101 --> 11:26.603
We haven't forgiven you yet,

11:26.854 --> 11:29.648
and I don't know if I ever will.

11:30.232 --> 11:33.402
But I think I understand
your situation a bit better now.

11:33.861 --> 11:37.489
I've made mistakes too, but
someone was there for me.

11:38.073 --> 11:41.410
Just like what Tsubaki's
doing for you guys.

11:41.743 --> 11:42.870
Kanji...

11:43.829 --> 11:45.622
Sorry, and thanks.

11:46.456 --> 11:47.916
You heard Kanji.

11:48.250 --> 11:49.710
I'll do anything to help too.

11:50.085 --> 11:50.878
So please,

11:51.336 --> 11:53.422
don't give up on
the things you love.

12:12.733 --> 12:14.443
Okay, I'm done.

12:15.611 --> 12:17.446
What kinda final
boss fight is this?

12:28.957 --> 12:31.627
- He's... done?
- What does that mean?

12:31.960 --> 12:34.087
Suzuri-san... lost?

12:39.176 --> 12:40.677
Thank you...

12:40.969 --> 12:43.096
Tsubaki-chan, Kan-chan...

12:45.557 --> 12:46.767
Suo-san.

12:47.768 --> 12:52.314
What do I do to get a
back as broad as theirs?

12:53.357 --> 12:56.235
I don't know much
about Kanji-san,

12:56.527 --> 13:01.240
but those two must've
been through a lot.

13:02.074 --> 13:05.244
That's probably why their
backs are so big and strong.

13:09.831 --> 13:11.207
H-Hey, wait!

13:11.208 --> 13:12.792
You shouldn't be moving yet!

13:12.793 --> 13:13.877
It's Suzuri.

13:14.878 --> 13:16.338
Shuhei Suzuri.

13:16.922 --> 13:18.131
And you guys?

13:18.382 --> 13:19.675
Kanji Nakamura.

13:19.925 --> 13:21.260
Tasuku Tsubakino.

13:21.718 --> 13:22.719
I see.

13:23.303 --> 13:24.388
Nakamura.

13:24.680 --> 13:25.681
Tsubakino.

13:26.223 --> 13:27.724
Can you give me a sec?

13:29.643 --> 13:31.144
I want to talk to them first.

13:37.734 --> 13:39.444
I wanted things to change.

13:40.112 --> 13:42.698
I wanted to leave that world where
we fought over a single cookie,

13:42.990 --> 13:45.742
where we could only
yearn for a better world.

13:46.201 --> 13:48.828
It didn't matter what we did,
as long as our bellies were full.

13:48.829 --> 13:51.081
I didn't care what
happened to anyone else.

13:51.498 --> 13:54.042
And I pushed you
guys down that path.

13:54.793 --> 13:56.712
But I knew...

13:57.171 --> 13:59.715
that it wasn't the right path.

14:00.549 --> 14:02.758
So I killed my emotions

14:02.759 --> 14:04.261
and pretended to be clueless.

14:05.053 --> 14:08.182
Because I thought that was
the only path I could walk.

14:09.558 --> 14:10.559
I'm sorry.

14:12.186 --> 14:16.815
I don't think I'll ever be able to
find a different path on my own.

14:17.316 --> 14:18.233
That's why...

14:18.650 --> 14:21.111
I want to follow the
path they showed me.

14:21.695 --> 14:24.448
I know I don't have
the right to say this,

14:25.282 --> 14:28.827
but won't you come with me?

14:29.328 --> 14:30.703
I want to...

14:30.704 --> 14:32.247
stay with you guys.

14:34.374 --> 14:36.126
The heck are you talking about?

14:37.252 --> 14:41.465
If it weren't for you, we'd all
be dead on the roadside by now.

14:41.715 --> 14:43.257
If that's what you want,

14:43.258 --> 14:45.093
then of course we're in!

14:45.511 --> 14:48.555
We're all one unit, right?

14:51.475 --> 14:54.228
We'll become one unit.

14:57.189 --> 14:58.315
Thanks.

15:02.653 --> 15:05.488
But can we even do it?

15:05.489 --> 15:06.489
What if we screw up—

15:06.490 --> 15:07.407
You dumbasses!

15:07.616 --> 15:10.576
Nobody's perfect
on their first try.

15:10.577 --> 15:12.412
Newbies will always
make mistakes.

15:12.663 --> 15:15.581
If newbies could do
everything from the start,

15:15.582 --> 15:18.043
we'd be jobless by now.

15:18.544 --> 15:20.711
And hey, with that
humility of yours,

15:20.712 --> 15:22.005
I'm sure you'll be fine.

15:22.840 --> 15:23.924
Suzuri.

15:26.343 --> 15:29.346
I see you lied to me.

15:29.763 --> 15:31.723
You said you had nothing,

15:31.974 --> 15:33.600
but that's clearly not true.

15:35.352 --> 15:36.728
Great job out there.

15:36.937 --> 15:39.147
Yeah, thanks for the help, guys!

15:43.485 --> 15:44.570
Kan-chan...

15:44.695 --> 15:46.696
Yo! I'm glad you're safe—

15:46.697 --> 15:48.407
- Tsubaki-chan—
- Do you...

15:48.699 --> 15:50.576
understand what you've done?

15:52.119 --> 15:56.498
You trampled over the
feelings of everyone here.

15:58.625 --> 15:59.625
C'mon, Tsubaki—

15:59.626 --> 16:00.919
Stay out of this, Kanji.

16:02.254 --> 16:05.257
I know that you care a lot
about Kanji and the others,

16:05.757 --> 16:08.010
and that you don't want
to cause trouble for them.

16:08.719 --> 16:13.348
But Kanji and everyone else
here care about you just as much.

16:14.266 --> 16:16.226
They want you to stay here.

16:16.560 --> 16:19.104
They know you want to be here,

16:19.688 --> 16:22.482
and they fought with all
they had to protect that wish.

16:23.775 --> 16:28.405
Sakura, Nirei, and Suo did their
best because of those feelings.

16:29.156 --> 16:32.784
And then you tried
to give yourself up.

16:33.660 --> 16:36.622
You made a choice that
would've broken everyone's hearts.

16:39.708 --> 16:43.544
Hey, hey, everything turned
out okay in the end, right?

16:43.545 --> 16:45.005
It's fine, Kan-chan.

16:45.380 --> 16:47.049
Tsubaki-chan's right.

16:47.758 --> 16:49.510
Sakura-kun also told me earlier,

16:50.010 --> 16:51.512
to take it all in.

16:52.763 --> 16:55.390
I didn't want to see
everyone getting hurt.

16:55.766 --> 16:58.560
But the truth was, I just
wanted to take the easy way out.

16:59.353 --> 17:01.395
I didn't have the resolve
to believe in everyone,

17:01.396 --> 17:03.857
or the resolve to make
my wish come true.

17:04.399 --> 17:06.026
Everything I did was half-baked.

17:06.276 --> 17:07.402
I'm horrible.

17:08.779 --> 17:10.447
I'm really sorry.

17:12.574 --> 17:14.409
Why didn't you say anything?

17:15.118 --> 17:17.996
I've always known you
were hiding something.

17:18.455 --> 17:20.415
But I thought I
didn't need to ask.

17:21.291 --> 17:24.753
I believed you'd tell me when
you were really in trouble.

17:25.546 --> 17:26.922
If you'd said something,

17:27.548 --> 17:29.508
I would've come to help anytime.

17:29.967 --> 17:32.052
When things get rough,
at least lean on me!

17:35.389 --> 17:37.765
If you ever start thinking
you're a burden again,

17:37.766 --> 17:39.184
you're not getting away easily.

17:40.060 --> 17:42.354
You have no idea...

17:42.729 --> 17:45.065
how much I love you!

17:50.737 --> 17:51.947
I'm sorry...

17:52.739 --> 17:54.157
I'm so sorry!

17:56.034 --> 17:57.160
Thank you...

17:57.661 --> 17:59.121
Tsubaki-chan...

18:03.876 --> 18:05.376
I know I said a lot,

18:05.377 --> 18:07.462
but that's enough serious talk.

18:07.754 --> 18:09.089
Next up...

18:09.673 --> 18:13.260
Go thank the guy who put himself
on the line for the girl he likes.

18:14.887 --> 18:17.471
Wh-Wha—the heck are you saying?!

18:17.472 --> 18:20.100
You two should just
get together already!

18:20.225 --> 18:21.642
Hey, don't rush them.

18:21.643 --> 18:23.478
They've got their own pace.

18:23.645 --> 18:25.688
No, Tsubaki's right.

18:25.689 --> 18:27.274
Just get together already!

18:27.441 --> 18:29.108
You'd make a good couple.

18:29.109 --> 18:30.484
Yeah, he's right.

18:30.485 --> 18:31.862
Right, Sakura-kun...

18:33.655 --> 18:37.241
Sakura-kun's romance
sensor isn't going off!

18:37.242 --> 18:40.077
You're right. He usually
goes beet-red at times like this.

18:40.078 --> 18:41.538
- Did he break—
- That ain't it!

18:43.040 --> 18:44.249
I was just thinkin'...

18:44.625 --> 18:47.211
I can't stand the
way you guys fight.

18:47.419 --> 18:49.337
W-Wait, Sakura-san?

18:49.338 --> 18:51.005
What's gotten into you?

18:51.006 --> 18:52.341
Suo-san?

18:55.677 --> 18:57.136
What do you mean?

18:57.137 --> 18:58.597
Tell me, Sakura.

18:59.473 --> 19:03.227
You said that whoever wins
or loses doesn't matter, right?

19:03.644 --> 19:05.311
That even if you all go down,

19:05.312 --> 19:07.856
what matters is that the
girl and the street are safe.

19:08.106 --> 19:09.483
Yeah, I did.

19:09.983 --> 19:13.946
At first, I thought it
was an amazin' mindset.

19:15.280 --> 19:17.741
But after being part of the
fight, I realized somethin'.

19:18.450 --> 19:22.037
I can't just stand by and
watch my allies go down!

19:22.454 --> 19:27.208
Even so, I know there's no
way where no one gets hurt.

19:27.209 --> 19:28.752
But I can't help it!

19:29.002 --> 19:30.462
I hate what I hate!

19:37.386 --> 19:40.013
Even I know that's
naive and unrealistic!

19:40.681 --> 19:43.015
Nah, everything's good.

19:43.016 --> 19:45.352
Keep that up, alright?

19:47.312 --> 19:49.856
Sure, it's not the best feeling,

19:49.857 --> 19:51.692
watching your guys go down.

19:52.401 --> 19:54.694
But even so, I learned
to look the other way

19:54.695 --> 19:56.989
for the sake of my objective.

19:57.573 --> 20:00.117
What you're saying
might be too idealistic.

20:00.367 --> 20:03.744
But if you can make
that ideal a reality,

20:03.745 --> 20:06.206
then that's obviously
the best outcome.

20:07.124 --> 20:08.584
You're fine the way you are.

20:09.126 --> 20:10.626
You're strong and smart.

20:10.627 --> 20:13.213
If you don't give up,

20:13.755 --> 20:16.341
you might actually
pull it off someday.

20:21.138 --> 20:22.805
You don't have to tell me that!

20:22.806 --> 20:25.892
Sakura-san! You felt
that way about us?

20:25.893 --> 20:27.351
I'm so happy, Sakura-kun.

20:27.352 --> 20:29.687
You'll protect me when
I'm in danger, right?

20:29.688 --> 20:32.858
The hell are you sayin'? You're
the last guy I expect to go down!

20:34.985 --> 20:36.527
They're so young.

20:36.528 --> 20:38.029
Nice, isn't it?

20:38.030 --> 20:40.281
Don't steal them
away from us now.

20:40.282 --> 20:41.532
No shit.

20:41.533 --> 20:44.369
I'm not dumb enough to
make a move on your favorites!

20:45.162 --> 20:50.501
Anyway, I can't wait
to see how he'll grow.

20:51.293 --> 20:52.293
Nakamura.

20:52.294 --> 20:54.129
Yeah? What's up?

20:54.546 --> 20:57.382
Again, I'm sorry
for what we did.

20:58.133 --> 21:02.971
You reached out to us despite what
we did, and we're grateful for that.

21:03.388 --> 21:05.807
From here on out, we
hope you'll take care of us.

21:08.477 --> 21:09.435
Sure.

21:09.436 --> 21:12.355
But, uh, I can't take
care of all of you!

21:12.356 --> 21:14.733
I kinda said that in the
heat of the moment, so...

21:15.108 --> 21:16.151
I know.

21:16.860 --> 21:19.780
We'll start by having the ones
who can work support the rest.

21:20.447 --> 21:22.407
After that, we'll
handle the rest.

21:23.158 --> 21:25.327
And Shizuka Narita,

21:25.702 --> 21:27.954
we're really sorry about today.

21:27.955 --> 21:29.498
S-Sure...

21:29.831 --> 21:34.795
I'm sure you won't
like us working here,

21:35.212 --> 21:36.713
and of course it'll scare you,

21:37.422 --> 21:41.008
so if you ever feel uneasy
with any of my guys,

21:41.009 --> 21:42.594
just tell me, no
matter how small it is.

21:43.303 --> 21:46.640
I'll take full responsibility
for everything they do.

21:47.516 --> 21:50.102
I promise they'll
never hurt you again.

21:53.313 --> 21:56.567
You're right that I'm scared.

21:57.359 --> 22:00.529
But I also understand how
hard it's been for you guys.

22:01.280 --> 22:04.240
More than anything,
I'm just like you,

22:04.241 --> 22:06.618
someone this town saved.

22:07.286 --> 22:10.204
I'm in no position to
say anything about

22:10.205 --> 22:12.164
you getting a helping hand

22:12.165 --> 22:14.001
or working in this town.

22:14.793 --> 22:19.882
So let's do our best
and repay Roppo Ichiza.

22:25.512 --> 22:26.597
Thank you.

22:28.682 --> 22:32.019
By the way, are you
guys gonna be okay?

22:32.186 --> 22:35.105
Didn't someone hire
you to kidnap Shizuka?

22:35.898 --> 22:36.899
Right.

22:37.900 --> 22:39.610
Ain't this bad?

22:39.776 --> 22:40.903
Don't worry.

22:41.278 --> 22:43.322
I'll talk to them
and make this work.

22:43.947 --> 22:45.365
"Talk," huh?

22:47.743 --> 22:50.953
Nobody's gonna listen
to what a loser has to say.

22:50.954 --> 22:53.123
You couldn't even
do your job properly.

22:53.790 --> 22:56.627
I really am a terrible
judge of character.

22:57.211 --> 22:58.336
Still,

22:58.337 --> 23:01.507
I managed to get my
hands on another Furin card.

23:02.633 --> 23:04.550
How'd he know we're from Furin?

23:04.551 --> 23:06.093
We're not in uniform.

23:06.094 --> 23:07.638
Why?

23:07.846 --> 23:10.098
Why are you here?!

23:10.307 --> 23:11.933
Oh, shut up.

23:11.934 --> 23:14.394
I can go wherever I want.

23:14.978 --> 23:17.231
Always has, always will.

23:17.523 --> 23:20.484
All of life's fun
and pleasures...

23:21.401 --> 23:26.365
are just a way to
kill time until you die.

23:26.990 --> 23:29.993
(Salvation)

23:30.577 --> 23:34.164
Tsubakino-san and Kanji-san
sure have broad backs.

23:34.706 --> 23:35.707
You think?

23:36.208 --> 23:38.501
Doesn't look that broad to me.

23:38.502 --> 23:40.962
That Hidaka guy
looks way bigger.

23:40.963 --> 23:42.630
Ah, I didn't
mean it like that...

23:42.631 --> 23:44.466
Actually, never mind.
